{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"BIT-valkey-2026-23631","published":"2026-05-07T11:51:58.626Z","modified":"2026-09-10T16:01:48.381058006Z","aliases":["BIT-keydb-2026-23631","BIT-redis-2026-23631","CVE-2026-23631","GHSA-8ghh-qpmp-7826"],"summary":"redis-server Lua use-after-free may allow remote code execution","details":"Redis is an in-memory data structure store. In all versions of redis-server with Lua scripting, an authenticated attacker can exploit the master-replica synchronization mechanism to trigger a use-after-free on replicas where replica-read-only is disabled or can be disabled, which may lead to remote code execution. A workaround is to prevent users from executing Lua scripts or avoid using replicas where replica-read-only is disabled. This is patched in version 8.6.3.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"valkey","ecosystem":"Bitnami","purl":"pkg:bitnami/valkey"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.2.13"},{"introduced":"8.0.0"},{"fixed":"8.0.8"},{"introduced":"8.1.0"},{"fixed":"8.1.7"},{"introduced":"9.0.0"},{"fixed":"9.0.4"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/bitnami/vulndb/tree/main/data/valkey/BIT-valkey-2026-23631.json"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}]}],"references":[{"type":"ARTICLE","url":"https://github.com/redis/redis/releases/tag/8.6.3"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/redis/redis/security/advisories/GHSA-8ghh-qpmp-7826"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23631"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:25216"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:25219"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:25925"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:26306"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:26540"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:33444"},{"type":"WEB","u